Minimum Duration: Some companies may require a minimum number of days for 
earned leave (for example, 3 days or more), though this can vary. 
In most companies, earned leave can be carried forward to the next year if not used 
within the calendar year, but there are usually limits on how many days it can be 
carried over. For example, some companies allow up to 30 days of accumulated 
leave to be carried forward, while others may allow. 
If earned leave is not used within the stipulated period or if there is a limit to how 
many days can be carried over, unused leave may lapse at the end of the year or upon 
termination of employment. 
Encashment of Earned Leave is a common practice in both the private and public 
sectors. If an employee has unused earned leave at the time of retirement or 
resignation, they are generally entitled to encash the unused earned leave.
